<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro de Mendoza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1487–<a href="/years/1537">1537</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro de Mendoza was a Spanish nobleman and conquistador to whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> granted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a> governorate in 1534. He led a large expedition that founded the first settlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> in 1536, but hunger and attacks by local peoples forced most settlers away. Ill, he sailed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1537 and died at sea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-de-mendoza.jpg" alt="Pedro de Mendoza" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Taken by the uploader, w:es:Usuario:Barcex · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buenos_Aires_-_San_Telmo_-_Parque_Lezama_-_20071215c.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
